    "explanation": "This ruling answers both sides. For the rider: your central ground is that the driver left the bay during the wait, so his two separate stays should not be added together. That ground fails on the policy's own terms. POL-NS-06(i) expressly permits separate in-geofence intervals within a single pickup attempt to be accumulated where the driver left and re-entered the arrival radius without going more than 300 m from the pin, AND a qualifying traffic advisory was in force. Both conditions are met here. EV-ADVIS-09107-01 is present and populated with type CLOSURE, its geometry covers the Orchard Central marked ride-hail bay, its active window (18:50-19:30) covers the waiting period (19:00-19:06:30), and the driver's furthest point during the excursion was 179.8 m - inside the 300 m leash. Adding the two runs (170 s from 19:00:00-19:02:50 and 160 s from 19:03:50-19:06:30) gives an accumulated in-geofence dwell of 330 seconds against the 300-second minimum for a LARGE_VENUE pickup, a 30-second surplus. Your point that the 170-second single unbroken run falls short is correct as far as it goes, but it is not the measure the policy uses once limb (i) is engaged. Your point that the 6.2-minute wait_time_min is wall-clock from the arrival marker and not the in-geofence hold is also correct, and for that reason we do not rely on it - the 330-second accumulated figure does the work. Your observation that POL-NS-06 turns on the driver's dwell and not on your presence is a correct statement of the clause, but POL-NS-06 only refunds where the dwell falls short, and it does not. For the driver: all four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold - the arrived event at 19:00:20 (limb a); the GPS trace placing you inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from the first fix at 19:00:00, before that event (limb b); the 330-second accumulated dwell (limb c); and termination by you with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW at 19:06:30, after the dwell elapsed, with no boarding event (limb d). Your arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05: at the marker timestamp you were stationary inside the arrival radius, not more than 300 m out and not travelling at 15 km/h or above. POL-NS-04 does not rescue the rider: limb (a) requires a locating or coordinating message from the rider, and the chat log's three messages are a SYSTEM notice and two of your own; in any event the rider's device sat a constant 519.4 m from the pin with zero qualifying fixes, well outside the 150 m rider presence radius. No artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08 - there is no clock skew, no sampling gap, the chat sequence is complete, and the SGD 4.00 fee reconciles exactly with the schedule (greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone fee and the RYDE_X tier fee, both SGD 4.00) - so no discount applies to the confidence. Compensation under POL-NS-07 is 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee, SGD 3.20, with the residual 20 percent as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: it requires both a count of 4 or more and a rate above 0.08, and no_show_terminations_30d is 1, so the first limb fails. On this ruling the rider's own charge stands and the amount shown moves as the driver's compensation, as POL-GEN-03 requires. No clause produces a referral, and no escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 is present."
